# Deck generation

When creating or editing files in `decks/`:

1. **Copy presets** from `presets/` — never build title or layout slides from scratch.
2. **Replace text only** — swap placeholder copy inside existing elements. Do not change structure, classes, stylesheets, or `../../` asset paths.
3. **Pick presets by name** — e.g. `deck-title-02`, `chapter-title-01`, `slide-02`. See `presets/README.md` and `presets/deck-titles/README.md`.

## File layout

```
decks/{deck-name}/
  deck-title.html
  slide-01.html
  slide-02-chapter-title.html
  slide-03.html
```

## Preset map

- **Title**: `presets/deck-titles/deck-title-01.html` … `deck-title-04.html`
- **Chapter**: `presets/chapter-titles/chapter-title-01.html`
- **Content**: `presets/content-slides/slide-01.html` (card grid), `slide-02.html` (alert stack)
- **Cards**: `presets/cards/quick-fact-card.html` (label + headline + meta inside `<card>`)

## Compile for presentation

Run the compiler after editing slide files. It auto-updates `slides.json` from every `.html` slide in the folder (excluding generated `index.html`), then writes `index.html`:

```bash
node scripts/compile-deck.js decks/{deck-name}
# or compile every deck:
node scripts/compile-all-decks.js
```

Open `decks/{deck-name}/index.html` to present. The `title` field in `slides.json` is preserved across syncs; the `slides` array is rewritten from folder contents (sorted by filename).
